1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,520
SpaceX is now selling weightlessness,
SpaceX 开始卖失重了，

2
00:00:02,520 --> 00:00:03,300
by the ton.
按吨卖。

3
00:00:03,300 --> 00:00:05,110
Meet Starfall: a flying saucer,
认识 Starfall：一个飞碟，

4
00:00:05,110 --> 00:00:06,630
about three meters wide.
大约三米宽。

5
00:00:06,630 --> 00:00:09,210
It carries up to a thousand kilograms of cargo
它能带最多一千公斤的货

6
00:00:09,210 --> 00:00:10,780
up to orbit and back home.
上太空，再带回家。

7
00:00:10,780 --> 00:00:12,810
It just hit the Hacker News front page,
它刚上了 Hacker News 首页，

8
00:00:12,810 --> 00:00:15,010
and people cannot stop arguing about it.
评论区吵个不停。

9
00:00:15,010 --> 00:00:19,200
Today's brain teaser: up there, gravity is still about ninety percent as strong.
今天的烧脑问题：在轨道上，重力还有地面的九成。

10
00:00:19,200 --> 00:00:20,830
So why does everything float?
那东西凭啥飘起来？

11
00:00:20,830 --> 00:00:21,980
Meet our hero, Saucy,
认识主角：小碟，

12
00:00:21,980 --> 00:00:24,120
a flat little capsule with a big job.
扁扁的小舱，干大活。

13
00:00:24,120 --> 00:00:25,670
The old way to get weightless:
老办法一：

14
00:00:25,670 --> 00:00:27,510
drop something down a tall tower.
从高塔上往下扔。

15
00:00:27,510 --> 00:00:29,230
You get a few seconds of float.
能飘几秒钟，

16
00:00:29,230 --> 00:00:30,070
Then, crunch.
然后，咣。

17
00:00:30,070 --> 00:00:32,580
Or ride a plane that dives like a roller coaster.
老办法二：坐飞机像过山车一样俯冲，

18
00:00:32,580 --> 00:00:35,930
About twenty seconds of float, then everyone feels heavy again.
飘大约二十秒，然后又变沉。

19
00:00:35,930 --> 00:00:38,360
SpaceX says Starfall gives you weeks of it.
SpaceX 说，Starfall 能给你好几周。

20
00:00:38,360 --> 00:00:39,550
Not seconds. Weeks.
不是几秒，是几周。

21
00:00:39,550 --> 00:00:41,420
Twist one: there is gravity in orbit.
反转一：轨道上有重力。

22
00:00:41,420 --> 00:00:45,120
At the space station, it is about ninety percent of what you feel here.
空间站那儿，重力还有地面的九成左右。

23
00:00:45,120 --> 00:00:47,300
Astronauts float because they are falling.
宇航员飘着，是因为他们在往下掉，

24
00:00:47,300 --> 00:00:48,100
All the time.
一直在掉。

25
00:00:48,100 --> 00:00:50,020
Picture Newton's cannon on a mountain.
想象山顶上有门牛顿大炮，

26
00:00:50,020 --> 00:00:52,460
Fire a ball, and it curves down to the ground.
打一发，球划个弧落地。

27
00:00:52,460 --> 00:00:54,130
Fire faster, it lands farther.
打得更快，落得更远；

28
00:00:54,130 --> 00:00:58,170
Fire fast enough, and the ground curves away as fast as the ball falls.
快到一定程度，地面弯下去的速度跟球掉的一样快。

29
00:00:58,170 --> 00:00:59,090
That is an orbit:
这就是轨道：

30
00:00:59,090 --> 00:01:01,150
falling forever, and always missing.
永远在掉，永远掉不到地上。

31
00:01:01,150 --> 00:01:04,650
In low orbit, that is about twenty eight thousand kilometers an hour.
低轨道大约每小时两万八千公里，

32
00:01:04,650 --> 00:01:07,310
Fast enough to cross America in about ten minutes.
我们算了下，十分钟左右横穿美国。

33
00:01:07,310 --> 00:01:09,170
When you and your lab fall together,
你和实验室一起掉，

34
00:01:09,170 --> 00:01:11,780
nothing presses on anything. That is weightless.
谁也压不着谁，这就是失重。

35
00:01:11,780 --> 00:01:13,120
So why pay for falling?
那花钱买“掉”图啥？

36
00:01:13,120 --> 00:01:15,750
Twist two: gravity messes up tiny crystals.
反转二：重力会把小晶体搅乱。

37
00:01:15,750 --> 00:01:17,680
Drug makers grow crystals of proteins
药厂要把蛋白质长成晶体，

38
00:01:17,680 --> 00:01:19,830
to see their shape and design medicine.
看清它的形状，才好做药。

39
00:01:19,830 --> 00:01:22,510
On Earth, warm liquid rises and cool liquid sinks.
在地面上，热的液体往上走，冷的往下沉，

40
00:01:22,510 --> 00:01:24,500
That churning is called convection.
这种翻滚叫对流。

41
00:01:24,500 --> 00:01:27,010
It is like a pot of soup that never stops churning.
就像一锅一直在翻滚的汤，

42
00:01:27,010 --> 00:01:28,500
The crystals come out lumpy.
晶体长得歪歪扭扭。

43
00:01:28,500 --> 00:01:31,340
In free fall, warm liquid has no up to rise toward.
一起自由下落时，热液体没有“上”可去，

44
00:01:31,340 --> 00:01:32,510
The soup goes calm.
汤就安静了。

45
00:01:32,510 --> 00:01:34,850
SpaceX says the crystals then grow smaller
SpaceX 说，这样晶体长得更小、

46
00:01:34,850 --> 00:01:35,920
and more uniform.
更整齐。

47
00:01:35,920 --> 00:01:38,280
Same idea for tissue grown from stem cells,
干细胞长的组织、

48
00:01:38,280 --> 00:01:39,940
and new materials for chips.
做芯片的新材料，也是这个道理。

49
00:01:39,940 --> 00:01:43,080
Saucy keeps the experiments plugged in: one kilowatt of power,
小碟让实验一直通着电：一千瓦，

50
00:01:43,080 --> 00:01:44,860
and a live link through Starlink.
还能通过星链实时联网。

51
00:01:44,860 --> 00:01:46,620
Twist three, the hardest part:
反转三，最难的部分：

52
00:01:46,620 --> 00:01:47,450
coming home.
回家。

53
00:01:47,450 --> 00:01:49,620
Saucy slams into the air at orbital speed,
小碟用轨道速度一头扎进大气，

54
00:01:49,620 --> 00:01:52,320
and the air in front gets crushed and blazing hot.
前面的空气被压得滚烫。

55
00:01:52,320 --> 00:01:53,940
Our guess: its wide, flat belly
我们猜：它又宽又扁的肚皮，

56
00:01:53,940 --> 00:01:55,620
works as a brake and a shield.
既当刹车，又当盾牌。

57
00:01:55,620 --> 00:01:56,640
It has flown twice,
它已经飞了两次，

58
00:01:56,640 --> 00:01:58,580
once in June and again in October.
六月一次，十月一次。

59
00:01:58,580 --> 00:02:01,120
Reports say three paying missions are already signed.
据报道，已经签了三单商业任务；

60
00:02:01,120 --> 00:02:03,780
The name comes from Starship, which would carry them.
名字里的 Star，来自要拉它们的星舰。

61
00:02:03,780 --> 00:02:05,590
Fine print: there is no price yet,
友情提示：还没有标价，

62
00:02:05,590 --> 00:02:08,210
so nobody knows how cheap affordable really is.
“便宜”到底多便宜，没人知道。

63
00:02:08,210 --> 00:02:10,190
And whether space-grown medicine pays off
太空里长的药值不值，

64
00:02:10,190 --> 00:02:11,320
is still an open bet.
也还是个没揭晓的赌局。

65
00:02:11,320 --> 00:02:13,320
Also, if you are hoping to ride along:
还有，想搭便车的：

66
00:02:13,320 --> 00:02:16,590
it is about seventy five centimeters tall. You will not fit.
它只有七十五厘米高，装不下你。

67
00:02:16,590 --> 00:02:18,580
So why does everything float in orbit?
所以，轨道上的东西凭啥飘？

68
00:02:18,580 --> 00:02:20,170
Not because gravity is gone.
不是因为没重力。

69
00:02:20,170 --> 00:02:22,200
Because everything is falling together,
而是大家一起在掉，

70
00:02:22,200 --> 00:02:23,880
and always missing the ground.
而且永远掉不到地上。

71
00:02:23,880 --> 00:02:26,030
SpaceX is not selling zero gravity.
SpaceX 卖的不是零重力，

72
00:02:26,030 --> 00:02:28,650
It is selling a very, very long fall.
是一次非常、非常长的坠落。

